# Wolseley Ten four-door saloon, 1939-1948.
#
# The 1,140 cc Ten: the small Wolseley of the war and immediate post-war
# years, with the Wolseley grille and six-light body. The museum car in the
# pack is a 1940 example.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_Ten
#
# Dimensions 3.734 x 1.448 x 1.55 m, wheelbase 2.286 m. The height is an
# estimate; no published figure was established.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-level side view from a museum, partly
# obscured by a rope in the foreground; the other images show the front and
# detail. The pack contains two different cars.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, grey, green and
# maroon are plain names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 110 km/h. Comfort 45/398, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 45. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1939 intro, retires staggered 1958-1961.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-ten.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/wolseley-ten.dae. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-ten/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear window corners and the wing-to-running-board
# transitions are too angular, and the museum photograph is partly obscured by a
# rope. At 128 px the six-light cabin, upright grille and small body read as a
# Wolseley Ten.


obj=citycar
name=WolseleyTen(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1939
intro_month=1
retire_year=1961
retire_month=6
speed=110
length=2
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=45
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=398

